    "body": "### Problem\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40531 breaks dirvish's `-` mapping and I don't see how the plugin can detect that it can safely clobber that mapping.\n\n----\n\nCopied from my comment on that PR:\n\nThis change makes it difficult for plugins to gracefully replace the `-` mapping because it uses an anonymous function. Plugins like [vim-dirvish](https://github.com/justinmk/vim-dirvish/) often use this pattern to avoid clobbering user mappings:\n\n```vim\nif mapcheck('-', 'n') ==# '' && !hasmapto('<Plug>(dirvish_up)', 'n')\n  nmap - <Plug>(dirvish_up)\nendif\n```\n\nmapcheck gives an unhelpful function ref (I assume this means it's the 10th function defined, so not a stable value):\n\n```\n:Verbose echo mapcheck('-', 'n')\n<Lua 10>\n```\n\ndefaults are processed before user configuration so `let g:loaded_nvim_dir_plugin = 0` in my config won't fix.\n\nHowever, using the raw plug mapping gives something that file navigation plugins can check for and ignore:\n\n```vim\n:lua vim.keymap.set('n', '-', '<Plug>(nvim-dir-up)')\n:Verbose echo mapcheck('-', 'n')\n<Plug>(nvim-dir-up)\n```\n\n> also fall back to the builtin - motion if the dir.lua is disabled, preventing mappings being made to undefined things\n\nCould we map nvim-dir-up to - in dir.lua in the disabled case instead?\n```lua\nif vim.g.loaded_nvim_dir_plugin ~= nil then\n  vim.keymap.set('n', '<Plug>(nvim-dir-up)', '-', { silent = true, desc = 'Go up one line' })\n  return\nend\n```\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\n-- Run this file:\n--    nvim --clean -u ~/.vim/repro_nvim.lua\n\nlocal cfg_root = \"~/nvim_issue_dirvish\"\n\nfor name, url in pairs {\n    sensible = 'https://github.com/tpope/vim-sensible.git',\n\n    dirvish = 'https://github.com/justinmk/vim-dirvish.git',\n} do\n    local install_path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(cfg_root .. '/pack/minimal/start/' .. name, ':p')\n    if vim.fn.isdirectory(install_path) == 0 then\n        vim.fn.system { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', url, install_path }\n    end\nend\nvim.opt.packpath:append(cfg_root)\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nDirvish is able to detect that it can override the built-in mapping.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-941+g7c9222f45e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, gvim 9.0.1576\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWin11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nn/a\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nn/a\n\n### Installation\n\nscoop",
